This effect is commonly known as a **Curtain Reveal** (or **Sticky Stacking / Sticky Reveal**). A section sticks in place within the viewport while the subsequent section slides up over it like a curtain covering it.

### Minimal CSS Implementation

You can achieve this natively using `position: sticky`:

```html
<section class="section sticky-panel">
  <h1>Sticky / Revealed Section</h1>
</section>

<section class="section curtain-panel">
  <h2>Curtain Section (Scrolls Over)</h2>
</section>
```

```css
* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
}

.section {
  min-height: 100vh;
  padding: 4rem 2rem;
}

/* 1. Sticks to top as you scroll */
.sticky-panel {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 1;
  background-color: #8c8c8c;
  color: #fff;
}

/* 2. Slides over the sticky section with higher stacking order */
.curtain-panel {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 2;
  background-color: #f7eed9;
  box-shadow: 0 -10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15); /* optional shadow edge */
}
```
